Article 35

(1) Special protection for children in conflict with the law as referred to in Article 3O covers children in conflict with the law and child victims of criminal acts, and is the obligation and responsibility of the government and society.

(2) Special protection for children in conflict with the law as referred to in paragraph (1) is implemented through: a. treatment of children in a humane manner in accordance with the dignity and rights of the child;

b. provision of special child companion officers from an early stage; c. provision of special facilities and infrastructure;

d. imposition of appropriate sanctions for the best interests of the child;

e. continuous monitoring and recording of the development of children in conflict with the law;

f. provision of guarantees to maintain relationships with parents or family; and

g. protection from disclosure of identity through the mass media and to avoid labeling.

(3) Special protection for children who become victims of criminal acts as referred to in paragraph (1) is implemented through: a. rehabilitation efforts, both in institutions and outside institutions; b. efforts to protect from disclosure of identity through the mass media and to avoid labeling;

c. provision of safety guarantees for victim witnesses and expert witnesses, both physical, mental, and social; and

d. provision of accessibility to obtain information regarding case developments.

Article 45

In addition to the rights of Persons with Disabilities as referred to in paragraph (1), children with disabilities have the right to:

a. receive special Protection from Discrimination, neglect, harassment, exploitation, and sexual violence and crime; b. receive family care and upbringing or substitute family care for optimal growth and development;
c. have their interests protected in decision-making; d. treatment of children in a humane manner in accordance with the dignity and rights of the child;
e. fulfillment of special needs;
f. equal treatment with other children to achieve social integration and individual development; and
g. receive social assistance.

